## BUGS

### B1: Timer bar missing task selector
The timer bar at the top only has description + project selector. There is no task selector in the timer bar. The spec says "Description field, project selector, task selector, tag selector inline in the timer bar." Without task selection, time entries started from the timer have no task assigned, making them less useful for reporting and for Phase 2 Jira integration.

### B2: Timer bar missing tag selector
No tag selector in the persistent timer bar. Tags can only be added after the fact via edit. This adds friction to the tracking workflow.

### B3: Dashboard "Today's Breakdown" doesn't update after timer stop
After starting and stopping a timer for "Web Application", the Today's Breakdown still shows "Web Application 0m". The dashboard stats ("Today 11h 21m") also didn't visibly refresh. The entry count updates (6->7->8) but the hours total stays stale. Either Turbo Stream updates are missing or the page needs a manual refresh.

### B4: Hourly rate input shows "cents" instead of dollars
New Project form shows "Hourly Rate (cents)" and "Budget Amount (cents)". Users should enter dollar amounts (e.g., $150.00), not cent values (15000). This is a UX issue -- store as cents internally but present as dollars to the user.

### B5: Budget Hours/Amount fields always visible
On the New Project form, Budget Hours and Budget Amount fields are visible even when "No Budget" is selected. These should be conditionally shown/hidden based on the Budget Type selection.

### B6: Time entry edit shows raw datetime format
The edit form shows "2026-03-12T16:21" in the Date & Start Time field. This is the raw HTML datetime-local format. While functional, it's not user-friendly. A friendlier date/time picker (Flatpickr is already in the spec) would be better.

