## UX IMPROVEMENTS

### U1: Timer bar should be more prominent when running
The timer bar changes to show REC + elapsed time when running (good), but the green accent is subtle. Consider making the entire navbar background change to a light green or adding a pulsing animation to make the running state unmistakable.

### U2: Timer description should persist after stop
When the timer stops, the timer bar clears the description and project. It would be better UX to keep the last description/project pre-filled so users can quickly start a similar entry.

### U3: Time entries need a "today" quick-scroll
When viewing time entries for the current week, there's a "Today" badge on Thursday's section, but if you scroll to older entries, there's no quick way to jump back to today. A floating "Back to Today" button would help.

### U4: Project color dots are too small in some views
On the Time Entries list, the project color dots are small and easy to miss. Making them slightly larger or using a color sidebar/border on each entry (like Toggl) would improve scannability.

### U5: Tags in time entry list are visually noisy
Tags appear as colored badges in the time entry rows, but when multiple tags are present, they compete visually with other elements. Consider a more subtle tag display (smaller, outline-only badges) or showing tags on hover/expand.

### U6: No keyboard shortcuts
Spec mentions keyboard shortcuts. No keyboard shortcuts are implemented. At minimum: S to start/stop timer, N for new entry, G+D for go to dashboard, G+T for go to time entries.

### U7: No empty state guidance
When a new user signs up and has no projects/entries, the dashboard will show 0s and empty lists. There should be onboarding guidance: "Create your first project", "Start tracking time", etc.

### U8: Timesheet cells should highlight on hover
The timesheet grid cells don't have hover state. Adding a hover highlight would make it clearer which cell you're about to edit.

### U9: No confirmation before deleting
Delete buttons on clients, tags, and time entries have no confirmation dialog. A single accidental click deletes data immediately.

### U10: Sidebar active state is subtle
The active page in the sidebar has a slightly different background but it's not very visible. Making the active state more prominent (stronger background, left border accent) would improve navigation awareness.

