## DESIGN IMPROVEMENTS

### D1: DaisyUI is not actually installed
The app uses Tailwind CSS (tailwindcss-rails gem is in the Gemfile) but there is no DaisyUI integration. The spec calls for DaisyUI as the design system. The current UI uses raw Tailwind classes, which means:
- No semantic component classes (btn-primary, card, stat, etc.)
- No theme system (corporate/business themes)
- No dark mode toggle capability
- More verbose and harder to maintain templates

Recommendation: Install DaisyUI and refactor to use its component classes.

### D2: Login/registration pages are plain
The auth pages work but are very minimal. A branded landing feel (app description, feature highlights, or at least a nice illustration) would improve first impressions.

### D3: No loading states
There are no loading indicators when performing actions (starting timer, saving entries, applying report filters). Turbo should show loading states for frame navigations.

### D4: Charts lack interactivity
The Summary Report pie chart and bar charts render but have no tooltips or click interaction. Chart.js supports hover tooltips out of the box -- they should be enabled.

### D5: Mobile responsiveness not tested
The sidebar uses a drawer pattern which should collapse on mobile, but mobile testing was not performed. The timer bar especially needs attention on small screens.

### D6: No favicon / app branding
The browser tab shows generic "Gold" text. A proper favicon and branded logo would improve the professional feel.

