## ARCHITECTURE CONCERNS FOR PHASE 2

### A1: Task selector needs searchable dropdown
Current task selector is a plain HTML <select>. For Phase 2 Jira integration, there could be hundreds of tasks per project. The task selector needs to be a searchable/filterable dropdown (e.g., Stimulus-powered combobox with search input). Build this in Phase 1.

### A2: Time entry description should support autocomplete
When developers start typing in the timer bar, suggest recent descriptions. This is useful now and essential for Phase 2 where Jira issue titles will be suggested.

### A3: No "My Tasks" panel on dashboard
The spec mentions a "My Tasks" panel for Phase 2 Jira integration. The dashboard layout should have a slot/section ready for this. Currently the dashboard has Today's Breakdown + Recent Entries. A third column or tab for "My Tasks" should be planned.

### A4: Per-task time recap not implemented
Spec says "build the query/scope for total time per task early". The project detail page shows recent entries but not a time recap grouped by task. This is the foundation for Phase 2's "how much time did I spend on PROJ-123" feature.

### A5: External reference fields exist but no UI
The database has external_reference, external_type, external_url on tasks and projects (good). But there's no way to see or manage these from the UI. Even a read-only display would be useful for debugging in Phase 1.

